{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":485722,"name":"David Stredansky","username":"David_Stredansky","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/david_stredansky/{size}/117231_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-07T19:24:42.130Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485722-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485722-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485722-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485722-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAgent Computer has been unusable for some time. Recovering hangs at “Getting ready” (0%) and never advances. Update Grok Bot’s Computer fails with:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe update couldn’t finish. Agent Computer is still on its previous image. Your files and logins are kept; installed apps and packages are not. Any agent turn that cannot pause is discarded.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWithout a working computer, Grok Bot is effectively useless (no computer use / takeovers).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eReset Grok Bot’s Computer also failed (just tried).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is not a Cursor Models quota issue: Spending shows Grok Bot weekly usage ~9%; Cursor Models is at 99% separately.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485722-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485722-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen Grok Bot 0.44.0 on Ubuntu, signed in with Cursor Ultra.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eComputer is unreachable / recovery needed.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eTry Recover computer → stuck on Recovering → Getting ready @ 0% (Continue in Background does not help).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFully quit all Grok Bot processes and relaunch → same.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSettings → Updates → Update Grok Bot’s Computer → Update failed (“still on its previous image”).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRepeat on phone hotspot (different network) → same Update failure / no fix.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSettings → Updates → Reset Grok Bot’s Computer → also failed.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485722-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485722-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRecover, Update, or Reset should finish and reconnect to a usable Agent Computer (or fail with a clear, actionable error). Prefer backend rebuild/reattach if the VM is stuck in a partial / previous-image state.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485722-operating-system-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485722-operating-system-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLinux\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485722-version-information-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485722-version-information-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot 0.44.0 (official .deb, amd64), Stable track\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485722-additional-information-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485722-additional-information-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAdditional Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNetwork checks (already done)\u003cbr\u003e\n*.us8.cursorvm.com wildcard DNS resolves on home Wi‑Fi and matches public DNS (1.1.1.1)\u003cbr\u003e\nHTTPS to \u003ca href=\"http://test.us8.cursorvm.com\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003etest.us8.cursorvm.com\u003c/a\u003e returns expected ELB 404\u003cbr\u003e\nSame failure on phone hotspot → unlikely local ISP DNS filter\u003cbr\u003e\nCursor IDE / api2.cursor.sh work normally on the same machine\u003cbr\u003e\nAccount\u003cbr\u003e\nCursor Ultra; Grok Bot weekly allowance available (~9% used)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAsk\u003cbr\u003e\nPlease check the Agent Computer for this account on the backend and rebuild/reattach if it’s stuck on a previous image or partial state. Client Update, Recover, and Reset have all failed. Happy to provide request IDs / timestamps if you tell me where to find them.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485722-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485722-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo - Cursor works, but with this issue\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-07T19:24:52.401Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":20,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":65.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":170957,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-0-44-0-linux-agent-computer-stuck-update-fails-with-previous-image-recover-hangs-at-getting-ready-0","display_username":"David Stredansky","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"http://test.us8.cursorvm.com","internal":false,"reflection":false,"clicks":1}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":132292,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-0-44-0-linux-agent-computer-stuck-update-fails-with-previous-image-recover-hangs-at-getting-ready-0/170957/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reac